{"texts": ["PR #147360: Revert \"Enforce single values when multi_value=no is configured on fields with doc values (#147071)\"\n\nReverts elastic/elasticsearch#147071.\n\nThis change is reverted to unblock CI. The newly added `mapping/40_doc_values_multi_value` YAML tests were failing deterministically on `bwc-snapshots` Part 6 in mixed-cluster tests that include 9.4.0 nodes \u2014 the `cluster_features: [\"mapper.doc_values.multi_value\"]` gate wasn't skipping the tests on mixed clusters where older nodes lack the feature, so the index request lands on a 9.4.0 node that silently accepts the document (`201 Created` instead of the expected `4xx`). The two `multi_value=no on multi-field {sub,parent} rejects parent array` scenarios both failed, and the subsequent cluster instability caused a cascade of `Connection refused` failures on other unrelated tests in the same task.\n\nEvery PR that rebased `main` after #147071 merged inherited this failure, making Part 6 red across the board.\n\nReproduced locally on `main` HEAD and confirmed that reverting clears the failure. See [build scan](https://gradle-enterprise.elastic.co/s/4qsrkpigs62vs) from PR #147321 for the CI signature."], "doc_ids": ["TARGET"], "vecs": [[-0.005947018973529339, -0.0050473823212087154, 0.01195574551820755, -0.010690350085496902, 0.06267165392637253, 0.06528399884700775, -0.004391444846987724, -0.015037157572805882, -0.039166953414678574, 0.04017513245344162, -0.052211251109838486, -0.03349508345127106, 0.020260389894247055, -0.02715206705033779, -0.04756495729088783, 0.05511199310421944, -0.01912921480834484, -0.08762289583683014, -0.021141039207577705, 0.0071435426361858845, 0.059125714004039764, -0.11373188346624374, -0.051384344696998596, -0.08460070937871933, -0.03742106631398201, -0.06771114468574524, -0.0575418584048748, -0.008234426379203796, -0.019087087363004684, 0.025530528277158737, -0.0027191031258553267, 0.031167278066277504, 0.09044982492923737, 0.03187128156423569, 0.026146331802010